## 1️⃣ Trending attractions in downtown Toronto (as of 2024)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s trending (2024) | Quick facts & highlights | Approx. distance from the city‑centre |
|---|------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| 1 | **CN Tower & EdgeWalk** | Still the iconic skyline‑defining landmark; the EdgeWalk (a hands‑free walk on the outer rim) has surged in popularity after the 2023 safety‑upgrade. | • Height: 553 m (1,815 ft)  <br>• Observation deck: 360° views, glass‑floor “SkyPod” <br>• EdgeWalk: 1‑hour experience, 116 m above ground | Central – right on Front St. W, 0 min walk from most downtown hotels |
| 2 | **Ripley’s Aquarium of Canada** | New “Deep‑Sea Tunnel” exhibit opened early 2024, drawing families and marine‑life enthusiasts. | • 20 000+ marine animals <br>• Interactive touch‑pools <br>• Located at the base of the CN Tower | 2‑minute walk from CN Tower |
| 3 | **Toronto Islands (Centre Island)** | “Island‑Breeze” ferry schedule expanded to 7 days/week in 2024; a popular day‑trip for picnics, bike rides, and skyline photo‑ops. | • 15‑minute ferry from Jack Layton Ferry Terminal <br>• Beaches, bike rentals, historic amusement park <br>• Great for sunset views over the city | 10‑minute ferry ride from the waterfront (near the CN Tower) |
| 4 | **Royal Ontario Museum (ROM)** | New “First Peoples” wing opened in spring 2024, boosting visitor numbers; consistently top‑rated on TripAdvisor. | • Over 6 million artifacts <br>• Highlights: dinosaur gallery, Indigenous art, Asian collection <br>• Open 10 am‑5 pm (closed Mon) | 15‑minute streetcar ride (or 10‑min walk) from the Financial District |
| 5 | **Distillery Historic District** | “Winter Lights Festival” runs through November, turning the cobblestone streets into a glowing art walk; boutique shops and craft‑brew pubs are buzzing. | • 19‑acre pedestrian‑only heritage area <br>• Galleries, design shops, restaurants <br>• Seasonal events & live music | 12‑minute streetcar ride (or 15‑min walk) from Union Station |

> **Tip:** All five attractions are within a 2‑km radius of Toronto’s central business district, so you can walk or hop on a quick streetcar between them.

